###### Abstract

We use time resolved spectroscopy of thermonuclear X-ray bursts observed from SAX J1748.9-2021 to infer the mass and the radius of the neutron star in the binary. Four X-ray bursts observed from the source with RXTE enable us to measure the angular size and the Eddington limit on the neutron star surface. Combined with a distance measurement to the globular cluster NGC 6440, in which SAX J1748.9-2021 resides, we obtain two solutions for the neutron star radius and mass, R=8.18\\pm 1.62 km and M=1.78\\pm 0.3 M{}_{\\odot} or R=10.93\\pm 2.09 km and M=1.33\\pm 0.33 M{}_{\\odot}.

